---

Stage 20 — Common Investigation Mistakes

Avoid

Judging complexity by unreadable identifiers.

Assuming renamed classes are unimportant.

Treating compiler-generated code as business logic.

Ignoring Android framework anchors.

Relying solely on decompiled names.

Skipping runtime validation.

Failing to document uncertainty.



---

Stage 21 — Packed, Protected & Obfuscated APK Methodology Master Checklist

By the end of this stage, you should be able to:

✅ Identify common transformation and protection characteristics at a high level.

✅ Recover architecture and subsystem responsibilities despite reduced readability.

✅ Build reliable call graphs, control-flow models, and data-flow models using stable framework anchors.

✅ Distinguish handwritten logic, compiler-generated infrastructure, and third-party libraries.

✅ Correlate resources, framework interactions, and runtime observations to improve semantic understanding.

✅ Maintain explicit confidence levels and evidence for every major conclusion.

✅ Produce professional documentation that accurately describes an application's architecture even when identifiers and code structure have been significantly transformed.



